3.3.0
* address page: the address's currency on the breadcrumb line, and a Currency panel (coin, ticker, name) or NFT panel (card face, ticker, name, linked to the card) before the figures; replaces "Deck cards seen"
* address page: Balance, Total received and Total sent carry the ticker, and shrink to stay on one line
* address page: Tx count is the address's whole history (it stopped at 100); /ext/getaddress returns currency and txcount
* SIS PoW reward follows the client's subsidy schedule (10 SIS since fork 5; it said 50)
* copy buttons for every transaction ID, block ID and address in the tables
* labels: Tx ID, Block ID, and Height for block heights, which lose their "#"
* shortened addresses keep their last six characters (the checksum), with the ellipsis in the middle
* card-page transaction links work (they pointed at a view that did not exist)
* phones: no zoom into the memo or search field, a shorter search hint, the Deck view and its controls fit the screen
* footer: "Powered by Iquidus" joins the copyright line; status bar block height in green
* Deck filter buttons in the site font
* README rewritten for Breakout; font licences and card-art provenance added

3.2.0
* Explorer tab refreshes every minute: new blocks slide into Latest blocks, and the supply, holders, difficulty and address figures update
* Explorer and Blocks tabs share one block table (height, age or time, type, block ID, txns, reward, forged by); block IDs link to the block, coloured by proof type
* status bar shows the tip's age and stays current on every page; it and the header stay at the top of the page
* address page: a bar with the address's Stealthicon, the address, and buttons for its QR code and Stealthicon
* QR code dialog, with the real QR code (it was a placeholder pattern), copyable and saveable as PNG
* Stealthicon dialog, with the mark and the canonical Stealthicons card (optional memo) copyable and saveable as PNG; Stealthicons library vendored
* copy buttons are an icon; Movement's Tx hash column is Tx ID
* footer: version as its own chip, link columns at natural width, sync figure moved to the Live chip

3.1.0
* /ext serves addresses, rich list, supply, distribution, transactions, blocks, movement and the Deck from the daemon's indexes
* movement ignores stake self-returns and change back to a sender; the cutoff follows settings.movement.min_amount
* removed MongoDB
* retired the Jade UI and the transaction views; the UI is public/thedeck.html
* rich list lists addresses, with the balance distribution charts beside it
* bounded idle RPC keep-alive connections
* version shown in the footer

3.0
* Breakout Explorer: multicurrency (BRK, BRX, SIS, The Deck) snapshot of the deployed tree

